  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Dutasteride is a 5-alpha-reductase inhibitor used to treat benign prostatic hypertrophy and, in some settings, male pattern baldness. It is an approved medicine, used mainly for urological conditions such as an enlarged prostate.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q424760&quot;>Wikidata Q424760</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>dutasteride</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>G04CB02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01126&quot;>DB01126</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/6918296&quot;>6918296</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:521033&quot;>521033</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q424760&quot;>Q424760</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C27H30F6N2O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>528.537 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
